Z||000008||DXR_DAD||09-21-2000||11:27 PM||||Frank that carpet was a *&@#% to get off. It was not in bad shape, the pass. side was perfect, so I thought I could save it   NOPE!<BR>I had to peel & cut it off. Man it was some good glue GM used!!!<P>Jeff that shifter pod was in near mint condition to start with so it was just covered over. It's the part of this project that I like best.And it gets lots of attention  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I just got the complete gauge console done today. Man it looks sweet<BR>I love the light gray  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Gold, It did not come with the door pockets<BR>but I did pick up a set for it, but the color is not a good match so I'm having a set made<BR>with the same vinyl as the door.<P>And I should give some props to my people at <BR>South City Auto Upholstery!!!!!! Any of you Bay Area FieroNs need work done go see Mike<BR>They are the best!!!!! Real Pros.<P>Mr. Mike's seats next on the list, I can't wait!!!<BR>I'll have pics soon as it's all finished<P>THANKS<BR>DXR_DAD <BR><p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 09-21-2000).]||||reg||14
